{"hint":"Hint: All numbers are stored in binary, how many 1s should a power of 2 have? Can you count the 1s?","title": "Powers of 2", "description":"<label>Problem #2: Power of two</label>\n            <p class=\"problemdescription\"> Powers of two are extrermely important in computer science, between binary numbers, binary trees, and recusrive algorithms like merge sort, they show up everywhere</p>\n            <br>\n            <p class=\"problemdescription\"> Find out if n is a valid power of 2</p>\n            <br>\n            <p class=\"problemdescription\"> 0 < n < 20000 will hold for all test cases find out if log_2(n) is an integer</p>\n            <br>\n            <p class=\"problemdescription\"> The number n will be stored at the memory address #fff0 before the start of execution store your result at address #ffff store 1 if it is a valid power, store 0 if it is not. You will have a maximum of 1,000,000 clock cycles for your program to finish execution</p>\n            <img src=\"2powers.jpg\"></img>","cases":[{"inputString":"1","outputString":"1","initial":[{"start":65520,"end":65521,"content":[1]}],"output":[{"start":65535,"end":65536,"content":[1]}]},{"inputString":"2","outputString":"1","initial":[{"start":65520,"end":65521,"content":[2]}],"output":[{"start":65535,"end":65536,"content":[1]}]},{"inputString":"3","outputString":"0","initial":[{"start":65520,"end":65521,"content":[3]}],"output":[{"start":65535,"end":65536,"content":[0]}]},{"inputString":"4","outputString":"1","initial":[{"start":65520,"end":65521,"content":[4]}],"output":[{"start":65535,"end":65536,"content":[1]}]},{"inputString":"5","outputString":"0","initial":[{"start":65520,"end":65521,"content":[5]}],"output":[{"start":65535,"end":65536,"content":[0]}]},{"inputString":"8","outputString":"1","initial":[{"start":65520,"end":65521,"content":[8]}],"output":[{"start":65535,"end":65536,"content":[1]}]},{"inputString":"9","outputString":"0","initial":[{"start":65520,"end":65521,"content":